Subject: conditional sidebarPanel based on tab
Message-ID: <5tcmeKAZ9mo.DLbyOXJnhVsJ@shiny-discuss.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/shiny-discuss/c/5tcmeKAZ9mo/m/DLbyOXJnhVsJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

I'd like to have different sidebar Panels be represented based on which tab I use currently. How I could implement it? Now I have

>  sidebarPanel(
>
>        conditionalPanel(condition="input.tabs=='Heatmap'",
>                        helpText("For tab \'Heatmap:\'")
>       ),
>         conditionalPanel(condition="input.tabs=='About'",
>                        helpText("For tab \'About:\'")
>       )
>
> )
>   mainPanel(
>     tabsetPanel(
>       tabPanel("Heatmap", textOutput("k"),plotOutput("heatmap",width = "1000px", height = "1000px"),value=1),
>       tabPanel("About", textOutput("about"),textOutput("about_test"),value=2)
>     )
>   )

But it doesn't work and I have the following error message

> Error in tabsetPanel(tabPanel("Heatmap", textOutput("k"), plotOutput("heatmap",  :
>   tabsetPanel doesn't have an id assigned, but one of its tabPanels has a value. The value won't be sent without an id.

Thank you in advance!

From u3be65e68ba76d9f5 at groups.google.com  Fri Mar  1 18:05:01 2013
From: u3be65e68ba76d9f5 at groups.google.com (Laszlo Szakacs)
Date: Fri, 01 Mar 2013 18:05:01 +0000
Subject: Re: conditional sidebarPanel based on tab
Message-ID: <5tcmeKAZ9mo.DlAUSF2B_zUJ@shiny-discuss.groups.google.com>
In-Reply-To: <5tcmeKAZ9mo.DLbyOXJnhVsJ@shiny-discuss.groups.google.com>
References: <5tcmeKAZ9mo.DLbyOXJnhVsJ@shiny-discuss.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/shiny-discuss/c/5tcmeKAZ9mo/m/DlAUSF2B_zUJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

You need an 'id' as the last parameter for 'tabsetPanel':

tabsetPanel(
  tabPanel("Heatmap", textOutput("k"),plotOutput("heatmap",width = "1000px", height = "1000px"),value=1),
  tabPanel("About", textOutput("about"),textOutput("about_test"),value=2)

  , id = "thisisanid"
)

Hope that helps, L

