Date: Thu, 07 Mar 2013 02:55:56 +0000
Subject: Re: Can someone please explain to me what "Passing functions to 'reactive' is deprecated." means
Message-ID: <IP7UwtB7Jhs.cEvo3EiZy-8J@shiny-discuss.groups.google.com>
In-Reply-To: <IP7UwtB7Jhs.KTvw0Nf1iMoJ@shiny-discuss.groups.google.com>
References: <IP7UwtB7Jhs.KTvw0Nf1iMoJ@shiny-discuss.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/shiny-discuss/c/IP7UwtB7Jhs/m/cEvo3EiZy-8J>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

You used to do this:

foo <- reactive(function() {
  data <- read.csv('foo.csv')
  subset(data, !is.na <http://is.na>(data$total))
})

With 0.4.0, you remove the "function()" part of it. The below is exactly equivalent to the above, only without the deprecation warning:

foo <- reactive({
  data <- read.csv('foo.csv')
  subset(data, !is.na <http://is.na>(data$total))
})

