I merged your improved code and added what I mean by "bidirectionnal".
It mainly concerns the renderValue, adding a trigger like this (in TableOutputBinding):
           onChange: function() { $(el).trigger('change');}
=>
 renderValue: function(el, data) {
      $(el).handsontable({
        data: JSON.parse(data),
        startRows: 5,
        startCols: 5,
        //minSpareCols: 1,
        //always keep at least 1 spare row at the right
        //minSpareRows: 1,
        //always keep at least 1 spare row at the bottom,
        autoWrapRow: true,
        rowHeaders: true,
        colHeaders: true,
        contextMenu: true,
        onChange: function() { $(el).trigger('change');}
      });

See in action : runGitHub("try-shiny","yannrichet",subdir="handsontable")

