Two issues here.

1) The <select> and <input type="checkbox"> both need id attributes, not name. (Or it's OK to have name, but you must also have id.)

2) If that alone doesn't fix it, try adding this after you set the selected index:
$("#fixed_float").change();

Please let me know if that works for you; if so, and you need further explanation about why that fixes it, I would be happy to explain.

Taking a step back, though, if you're presenting two mutually-exclusive sets of inputs or outputs, you might be better served with using tabsetPanel <http://rstudio.github.com/shiny/tutorial/#tabsets> (note that if you give tabsetPanel an inputId, then your R code can know which tab is active); and if you prefer not to use tabsetPanel, then at least checkboxGroupInput for the Fixed/Float choice and use conditionalPanel <http://rstudio.github.com/shiny/tutorial/#dynamic-ui> to hide/show the relevant controls. As far as I can see, everything you want to do here can be accomplished entirely using Shiny features, no JavaScript required.

